<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nabu-mukin-apli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 978–943 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nabu-mukin-apli was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> from about 978 to 943 BCE and the first ruler of the Dynasty of E. His long reign was troubled by Aramean incursions, and the chronicles record that in several years the New Year festival could not be held because the road to Babylon was cut. He was succeeded by his son Ninurta-kudurri-usur II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nabu-mukin-apli.jpg" alt="Nabu-mukin-apli" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: L. W. King · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nab%C3%BB-mukin-apli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
